                                        <div class="modal-body"><p>PGDTRBS holders will be equipped to serve various Government and NGOs dealing with Social work, tribal studies, tribal health and other related developmental activities Sectors. Fresh graduates who complete this programme will be the potential candidates suitable for employment at the grassroots, supervisory and other middle level positions in the Tribal development, Tribal population, health and other development departments. The programme also strengthens the efficiency and effectiveness of in-service personnel working in government and non-government organizations, private or corporate sectors and handling various tribal development programme and other development projects and programmes. In-service professionals with PGDTRBS will be more potential candidates suitable for higher level positions in the social welfare officer, educationists, health worker and other development issues and challenges in the society/ corporate social responsibility fields, UNFPA, UNDP, WHO, ILO, UNICEF, Women and gender study, health insurance, etc. In addition, they can act as more resourceful persons in the field of Tribal studies. It also provides scope for those interested in establishing a local voluntary organization / NGO as a part of their self-employment and greater involvement in development.</p></div>
